 What is FileServer?
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 If you are like me, you'll get a lot of 'Numb' users. Now I've only been at
 this but a short while, and I've found that some User's get all in a tiswas
 when it comes down to finding important Files, like the Files Lists etc.

 So I decided to write this little Utility to help mainly the NewUsers, but
 then thought what a good Idea for experienced User's aswell.

 It detects for NewUsers (Access 1) then serves them with an option to
 Download your Files list or whatever while logging onto the BBS (they dont
 have to take 'em:() 

 If it detects a User logging in with an Access level higher than (Access 1)
 it serves them a different Menu, so they can select from the list provided,
 again they are not forced to take a file:)

 FileServer will if requested, Mark and downLoad the Files, before finishing
 the login sequence. 


 Installation
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~
 Easy! 

 1. Put as is, in Doors:FileServer/

 2. You will need to Edit some of the defaults in FileServer.rexx, in order
    for the proggy to know the Names of your files etc:) I have made them a
    lot simpler to edit now.)

 3. I assume Doors: is assigned? 
    In TEXT.WELCOME.USER put \#0Doors:FileServer/FileServer.rexx\
    I am using Shuttle Login on my BBS and also put 
    \#0Doors:FileServer/FileServer.rexx\ as the last line in my 
    NU.QUESTIONS.SYSOP file, that way, applying NewUsers can also 
    download my File List, even though they can't get on the BBS:) 

 4. Instead you could always add it to your EX.BBSMenus as:
    580,          FD,              0,           "1-32",           "\#0Doors:FileServer/FileServer.rexx\"
    Put a command in ya Main Menu as (FD) Free D/Loads. 
    Using 580 would make it a Global Command of course:)

 5. There is also a script and a CronTab supplied with this version. This
    is to keep Sysop's work to a minimum. You will need to edit the Script
    in order for the Cron to find the files to copy. The Cron is set to run
    at 12.15am, if this conflicts with other Crons etc, then I suggest you
    Edit this also.....

 Useage
 ~~~~~~
 It's all Automatic, I'm using Joylist to generate the lists, but I guess
 any list/lists will do.............. 

 The file selected is marked for the user and the download sequence is
 started. No creds are used, so its a free download, can't be bad eh!

 Entries are made to the Callers Log, even when a Newuser declines the Files
 List:( No entry is made if a user with Access above 1 declines to take
 anything.
 
 And thats all there is to it really, simple but user friendly, the feedback
 so far is "The Users Love it", Thats what I like to hear:))))))))))


